        <h2 class="content-title">Best Time, Cost and Getting There</h2>
        <div class="title-divider"></div>
        <p><strong>Best time:</strong> October and November give the clearest views from every viewpoint, and March to May brings rhododendrons into bloom through the forests. From December to February, snow can close the Khayer Lake trail and make Mardi Himal High Camp very cold.</p>
        <p><strong>Cost:</strong> the trek costs $999 to $1,199 per person depending on group size. It includes private transport, permits, meals, accommodation, and guide and porter. See the cost table.</p>
        <p><strong>Getting there:</strong> we drive from Pokhara to Kande in about an hour and start walking the same morning. The trek ends at Banau, with a drive back to Pokhara via Kushma.</p>
        <p><strong>What to bring:</strong> you will sleep above 3,500 m on several nights, so pack proper warm layers. Our <a href="/what-to-pack-for-khopra-ridge-trek">Khopra Ridge packing list</a> covers everything you need for this route too.</p>
        <p><strong>Comparing routes?</strong> Read why the <a href="/multiple-viewpoints-trek-alternative-to-annapurna-circuit">Multiple Viewpoints Trek is the best alternative to the Annapurna Circuit</a>. Short on time? The <a href="/khopra-ridge-trek">Khopra Ridge Trek</a> covers the second half in 8 days, and the <a href="/kokhe-danda-trek">Kokhe Danda Trek</a> covers Parbat in 5.</p>
      </div>

